auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiToken}}
}

docs {
  # Medispeak v2 API

  Async, metered, multi-tenant public API. Full reference: docs/api/v2.md.

  Flow: create a scribe session declaring outputs -> upload audio (or a
  document) -> commit (billable, idempotent) -> poll GET /:id until the HTTP
  status is 200/206 (202 means still processing), or receive the webhook.

  Every request authenticates with `Authorization: Bearer {{apiToken}}`
  (an `msk_live_...` account token minted on /api_tokens). Set `apiToken`
  and `baseUrl` in the environment.

  The "Create Session" and "Mint Session Token" requests store `sessionId`
  and `sessionToken` env vars from their responses so the rest of the
  collection chains without copy-pasting ids.
}
